## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Readycheck |cff33ff99World|r
## Notes: Everything world buff: drop timers, the timer network, the buff board, pull timer bars, auto turn-ins and summon automation.
## Author: Zac
## Version: 1.0
## Dependencies: Readycheck
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Head_Dragon_01

# Three layers that all concern world buffs, kept in one addon so they
# can be turned off as a unit:
#   WorldTools   local detection, pull timer bars, turn-ins, summons
#   WorldBuffs   the guild timer network and map pins
#   the board    who in your group has what, synced over the mesh
#
# ALL SETTINGS STAY IN ReadycheckDB (worldTools, worldBuffTimers,
# worldBuffs, worldBuffCache). They belong to the main addon on purpose:
# disabling this layer must not throw a single setting away, and
# re-enabling it has to pick up exactly where it left off.
#
# The main addon reaches in from three places, every one already written
# as a nil-guard so it no-ops when this addon is off:
#   Mesh_Inbound   -> RC.WorldBuffTimers.Mesh (WBTIME / WBYELL commands)
#   Mesh_Inbound   -> RC.WorldBuffs peer records
#   Core_Scan      -> RC.WorldBuffs diagnostics, CS_Gold -> peer gold

# ---------- World Tools ----------
# Core defines RC.WorldTools and the settings store the rest read
# through, so nothing here moves above it.
WorldTools\WT_Core.lua
WorldTools\WT_Timers.lua
WorldTools\WT_Turnins.lua
WorldTools\WT_Bars.lua

# ---------- World buff timer network ----------
# Core defines RC.WorldBuffTimers and its store. Detect drives the pull
# timer bars above via RC.WorldTools.Bars, so WT_Bars must already exist.
WorldBuffs\WBT_Core.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_CityNpcs.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_Comms.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_Detect.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_Mesh.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_MapPins.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_Hooks.lua

# ---------- Buff board ----------
# Publishes RC.WorldBuffs, which the board UI below reads.
WorldBuffSync.lua

# ---------- UI, last ----------
# These register sidebar pages and read the tables built above.
WorldTools\WT_UI.lua
WorldBuffs\WBT_UI.lua
UI\SidebarWorldBuffs.lua
